00;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">PRIMARY</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Ideal for dust, smoke, light leaks, and embers.</span></p></td></tr><tr style="height:0pt"><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:93.6pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">WebGL Particle Engine</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;(Three.js Points)</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:93.6pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Headless Chromium</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:93.6pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Medium (~350 ms/s)</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:93.6pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">High (Seeded PRNG)</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:93.6pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Reserved for 3D scenes requiring depth collision.</span></p></td></tr><tr style="height:0pt"><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:93.6pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Remotion HTML Canvas 2D</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:93.6pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Headless Chromium</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:93.6pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">High (~1200 ms/s)</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:93.6pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">High (Seeded PRNG)</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:93.6pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Discouraged due to high CPU load during batch renders.</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span>Building a custom procedural particle simulation engine adds unnecessary complexity. Atmospheric effects are best handled using </span><span style="font-weight:700">pre-rendered ProRes 4444 alpha plates</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;or high-resolution black-background plates blended via FFmpegâ€™s blend=all_mode=screen or addition modes. This approach ensures high visual quality, maintains frame determinism, and executes with minimal compute overhead during final compositing.</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">13. AI-Assisted Motion</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Generative AI video models (e.g., Wan2.1, Kling, CogVideoX, LTX-Video) synthesize temporal motion from static images. While capable of generating organic movement, their operational characteristics limit their viability as default motion engines:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_9-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Lack of Precise Camera Control</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Generative video diffusion models do not follow sub-pixel camera contracts. A prompt requesting a "slow 5% zoom to coordinates (0.62, 0.45)" frequently results in camera drift, unwanted perspective changes, or subject distortion.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Generation Latency and Cost</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Synthesizing five seconds of video with modern diffusion models requires 20 to 60 seconds on enterprise GPUs (such as the Nvidia A100 or H100), incurring significant compute expenses. In contrast, deterministic 2D and 2.5D transformations execute in under 500 milliseconds on standard CPU workers.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Role in Production</span><span>: AI motion should be reserved as a </span><span style="font-weight:700">specialized fallback</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">. It is invoked only when narrative intent requires non-rigid physical transformationsâ€”such as water ripples, drifting clouds, fluttering fabric, or historical portrait animations (e.g., eye blinks and subtle facial movement)â€”that cannot be modeled with geometric transformations.</span></li></ul><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">14. Motion Contract</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The Motion Contract is a normalized, renderer-agnostic JSON data structure exchanged between the Motion Planner and downstream render workers. It specifies the timing, spatial coordinates, easing equations, and asset bindings required to execute a shot without referencing engine-specific syntax.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Courier&quot;;font-style:normal">{<br> &nbsp;"$schema": "https://schema.engine.internal/v1/motion-contract.json",<br> &nbsp;"contract_id": "mot_cinematic_push_089a",<br> &nbsp;"scene_id": "scene_act1_intro",<br> &nbsp;"duration_frames": 150,<br> &nbsp;"fps": 30,<br> &nbsp;"canvas": {<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"width": 1920,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;"height": 1080<br> &nbsp;},<br> &nbsp;"tracks": [<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;{<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"track_id": "bg_visual",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"type": "IMAGE_TRANSFORM",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"asset_ref": "asset_img_archival_warroom_01",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"motion": {<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"primitive": "PAN_ZOOM",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"easing": "CUBIC_BEZIER",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"easing_params": [0.25, 0.1, 0.25, 1.0],<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"start": { "center_x": 0.50, "center_y": 0.50, "scale": 1.00, "rotation_deg": 0.0 },<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"end": &nbsp; { "center_x": 0.55, "center_y": 0.42, "scale": 1.15, "rotation_deg": 0.0 }<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;}<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;},<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;{<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"track_id": "atmospheric_fx",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"type": "OVERLAY_PLATE",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"asset_ref": "plate_fx_dust_motes_loop",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"blend_mode": "SCREEN",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"opacity": 0.45<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;},<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;{<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"track_id": "caption_layer",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"type": "KINETIC_TYPOGRAPHY",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"transcript_ref": "transcript_segment_act1_01",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"style": {<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"font_family": "Inter Display",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"font_weight": 700,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"font_size_px": 64,<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"color_active": "#FFD700",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"color_inactive": "#FFFFFF",<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"animation": "BOUNCE_HIGHLIGHT"<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;},<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;"safe_zone": { "anchor": "BOTTOM_CENTER", "margin_y_px": 140 }<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;}<br> &nbsp;]<br>}<br></span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">This contract schema provides key operational advantages:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_a-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Minimalist Field Definitions</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: The schema uses normalized floating-point coordinates ([0.0, 1.0]) rather than fixed pixel offsets, ensuring motion parameters scale consistently across different output resolutions (e.g., 1080\text{p}, 4\text{K}, or vertical 9:16).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Engine-Agnostic Structure</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: The contract can be parsed by an FFmpeg filtergraph generator, a Remotion composition loader, or a WebGL shader runtime without altering upstream planning logic.</span></li></ul><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">15. Motion Planning vs. Rendering Separation</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">To maintain architectural stability and prevent vendor lock-in, the production engine enforces a clear operational boundary between creative intent, parameter calculation, and pixel rendering:</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Courier&quot;;font-style:normal">Hermes Orchestrator (Creative Intent)<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”‚<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”‚ Semantic Directive: "Slow, somber push-in on Churchill's face"<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â–¼<br>Motion Planner (Geometric Calculation)<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”‚<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”‚ Computes bounding boxes, safe margins, and BÃ©zier curves<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â–¼<br>Normalized Motion Contract (JSON)<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”‚<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”‚ Typed, renderer-agnostic motion parameters<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â–¼<br>Motion / Graphics Workers (Pixel Rendering)<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”œâ”€â”€ FFmpeg Worker: Sub-pixel image transforms &amp; raster blending<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”œâ”€â”€ Remotion Worker: Kinetic typography &amp; vector overlays<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â””â”€â”€ WebGL Worker: Multi-plane 2.5D parallax displacement<br></span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Operational Separation</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_b-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Hermes Orchestrator</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Operates purely on narrative context, dramatic tension, and editorial pacing. It does not calculate pixel coordinates, resolution scaling, or frame counts.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Motion Planner</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Translates semantic intent into explicit mathematical parameters. It evaluates asset dimensions, applies easing curves, verifies safe zones, and generates the normalized Motion Contract.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Motion Workers</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Modular renderers that ingest the contract and output finished frames using specialized tools (FFmpeg, Remotion, WebGL).</span></li></ul><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">16. Asset-Aware Motion</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Applying hardcoded motion parameters to uninspected assets can introduce noticeable framing errors, such as cutting through a subject's face, panning into empty space, or obscuring focal points behind subtitles.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The Motion Planner uses a lightweight computer vision pipeline to inspect assets before generating motion parameters:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_c-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Focal Saliency and Face Detection</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Using lightweight vision models (e.g., YOLO-World or MediaPipe), the planner extracts normalized bounding boxes [x_{\min}, y_{\min}, x_{\max}, y_{\max}] for primary subjects and faces.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Headroom and Framing Offsets</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: The cameraâ€™s terminal target coordinate (\text{center\_x}, \text{center\_y}) is anchored to the detected subject, offset upward by 10\% to maintain natural cinematic headroom.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Canvas Boundary Clamping</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: To prevent black borders from appearing during zoom and pan operations, coordinate offsets are constrained mathematically by the scale factor: \text{scale} \ge 1.0, \quad \frac{0.5}{\text{scale}} \le \text{center\_x} \le 1.0 - \frac{0.5}{\text{scale}}</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Subtitle Collision Clearance</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: The planner checks the coordinates of primary subjects against subtitle safe zones. If a subject occupies the lower third of the canvas, captions automatically shift to the upper third to prevent visual overlap.</span></li></ul><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">17. Compositing</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Compositing combines base video assets, graphical overlays, typography plates, and atmospheric effects into a final rendered sequence. The workload is partitioned across rendering tools based on operational strengths:</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Courier&quot;;font-style:normal">Compositing Workload Partitioning<br>â”‚<br>â”œâ”€â”€ Native FFmpeg Filtergraph (High-Throughput Pixel Operations)<br>â”‚ &nbsp; â”œâ”€â”€ Base video stream sequencing<br>â”‚ &nbsp; â”œâ”€â”€ Environmental plate blending (Screen, Additive, Multiply)<br>â”‚ &nbsp; â”œâ”€â”€ Color grade applications (3D LUT mapping via .cube files)<br>â”‚ &nbsp; â””â”€â”€ Chroma keying and luma keying with edge erosion<br>â”‚<br>â””â”€â”€ Remotion Headless Worker (Dynamic DOM Layout Operations)<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;â”œâ”€â”€ Kinetic subtitle overlays[span_242](start_span)[span_242](end_span)[span_244](start_span)[span_244](end_span)<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;â”œâ”€â”€ Animated vector lower thirds and callout graphics<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;â”œâ”€â”€ Dynamic text wrapping and layout refl[span_228](start_span)[span_228](end_span)[span_234](start_span)[span_234](end_span)ow<br> &nbsp; &nbsp;â””â”€â”€ Transparent alpha stream output (ProRes 4444 / raw RGBA pipe)<br></span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">By isolating graphical layout tasks within Remotion and routing video plate blending to FFmpeg, the engine avoids the memory and CPU overhead of processing heavy base video streams inside a headless browser.</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">18. Performance and Scaling</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Rendering efficiency dictates infrastructure costs and throughput when scaling automated video production. Workloads are distributed across specialized compute tiers to optimize resource usage:</span></p><table style="border-spacing:0;border-collapse:collapse;margin-right:auto"><thead><tr style="height:0pt"><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:sol