style="font-weight:700">Secondary</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: libass via FFmpeg subtitles filter, reserved for simple, static subtitle tracks.</span></li></ul><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Vector Motion Graphics &amp; Infographics</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_11-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Primary</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Remotion SVG (@remotion/paths) paired with React chart libraries. Enables declarative vector path animation, dynamic layout sizing, and programmatic chart rendering.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Secondary</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: ThorVG C++ library for high-speed Lottie badge and icon rendering.</span></li></ul><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">2.5D Parallax &amp; Depth Synthesis</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_12-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Primary</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Depth Anything V2 (Small model) or V3 paired with BiRefNet segmentation and Three.js WebGL canvas displacement. This combination delivers clean foreground/background separation and controlled camera movement under commercially permissive licenses.</span></li></ul><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">High-Throughput Layer Compositing</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_13-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Primary</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Native FFmpeg filtergraphs (overlay, blend, lut3d). Provides hardware-accelerated pixel compositing and color grading with low CPU overhead.</span></li></ul><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">23. Targeted Validation Queue</span></h2><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The following structured experiments are designed to validate specific engineering hypotheses within the production environment:</span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Experiment 1: Sub-Pixel Trajectory Smoothness Validation</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_14-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span>*</span><span style="font-style:italic">Hypothesis</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">*: Standard FFmpeg zoompan produces measurable pixel stepping jitter on slow zooms over 5 seconds, whereas Remotion CSS transforms and OpenCV getRectSubPix maintain smooth sub-pixel continuity.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Exact Test</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Render a 150-frame, 5-second slow push-in (zoom scale 1.00 to 1.05) on a fine-line resolution test grid (1920\times1080 @ 30fps) across three pipelines: (a) FFmpeg zoompan, (b) FFmpeg 4K oversampled crop, (c) Remotion CSS scale(), and (d) OpenCV getRectSubPix.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Evidence Required</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Frame-by-frame centroid displacement metrics extracted from image differences; visual inspection of edge oscillation.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Success Criteria</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Centroid displacement must exhibit a monotonic linear curve with mean squared error variation &lt; 0.05 pixels across adjacent frames.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Why Research Evidence is Insufficient</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Trac ticket #4298 identifies the bug, but whether modern FFmpeg builds using floating-point expressions mitigate the issue on real-world photo assets requires empirical verification.</span></li></ul><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Experiment 2: Deterministic WebGL Map &amp; Chart Frame-Stepping</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_15-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Hypothesis</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Headless Chromium instances running MapLibre GL JS inside Remotion can achieve 100% byte-for-byte frame identity across repeated renders when initialized with fadeDuration: 0 and ANGLE backends.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Exact Test</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Render 300 frames of a dynamic MapLibre route fly-through twice on the same host machine across separate runs. Compute SHA-256 hashes of all exported PNG frames between Run 1 and Run 2.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Evidence Required</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Complete list of 300 SHA-256 frame hashes from both runs.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Success Criteria</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Identical hash matches across all 300 sequential frames (100\% match rate).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Why Research Evidence is Insufficient</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Community examples show deterministic map rendering, but real-world GPU driver micro-variations and network tile caching in headless Linux Docker environments can introduce subtle frame timing drift.</span></li></ul><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Experiment 3: ThorVG vs. Lottie-Web Server-Side Throughput</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_16-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Hypothesis</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Rendering Lottie animations natively via the ThorVG C++ library executes at least 4\times faster with lower memory consumption than rendering through lottie-web inside headless Chromium (@remotion/lottie).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Exact Test</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Benchmark export of a 10-second complex vector Lottie file (containing 5,000 primitives and drop shadows) to raw RGBA frame sequences at 1080\text{p} 60fps using (a) ThorVG CLI/bindings and (b) Remotion headless Chromium.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Evidence Required</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Total wall-clock execution time, peak memory usage (RSS MB), and CPU load graphs.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Success Criteria</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: ThorVG executes frame rasterization in &lt; 25\% of the wall-clock time required by Chromium.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Why Research Evidence is Insufficient</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: ThorVG documentation publishes raw draw call benchmarks, but integrated video pipeline throughput with disk/pipe streaming has not been verified in this environment.</span></li></ul><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Experiment 4: Monocular Depth Parallax Boundary Tearing</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_17-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Hypothesis</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: A two-plane parallax scene (BiRefNet foreground cutout + fast diffusion background inpainting) rendered in Three.js produces acceptable visual fidelity for documentary video without the multi-minute overhead of Layered Depth Inpainting (LDI).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Exact Test</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Ingest 20 diverse historical documentary stills. Generate foreground masks with BiRefNet, inpaint occluded backgrounds via LaMa, mount both on offset Z-planes in Three.js, and execute a 3-second camera orbit (5^\circ Y-axis rotation). Conduct blind evaluation for boundary tearing and rubber-sheet stretching.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Evidence Required</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Mean execution latency per image; human visual evaluation scores across boundary quality and realism.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Success Criteria</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: End-to-end asset prep and rendering completed in &lt; 5.0 seconds per image with zero visible background tearing.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Why Research Evidence is Insufficient</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Academic papers demonstrate high-end 3D photo inpainting, but real-world visual acceptability thresholds for fast two-plane planar approximations in YouTube documentary formats remain unquantified.</span></li></ul><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">24. Genuine Architectural Gaps</span></h2><ol class="lst-kix_list_18-0 start" start="1" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Sub-Pixel FFmpeg Motion Adapter</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Standard FFmpeg lacks a native filter that combines floating-point crop calculation with sub-pixel interpolation. A lightweight Python or C-extension worker using OpenCV (cv2.getRectSubPix) is required to generate smooth pan/zoom sequences without coordinate jitter.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Typography Layout Compiler</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: While @remotion/captions parses word timestamps, an automated planning adapter is needed to translate Pass 4F transcripts into safe-zone-constrained, line-wrapped visual cards that dynamically avoid collisions with visual subjects.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Automated Visual Saliency Worker</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: A standardized computer vision micro-worker is needed to inspect resolved images, detect human faces and focal regions, and output normalized bounding boxes that constrain camera zoom targets automatically.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Transparent Graphics Interceptor</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: An optimized frame piping interface between Remotion (Node.js/Chromium) and FFmpeg that avoids writing gigabytes of intermediate uncompressed PNG frames to disk, relying instead on shared memory or named UNIX pipes (y4m / raw RGBA).</span></li></ol><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">25. Recommended Motion / Compositing Architecture</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The end-to-end motion and compositing architecture operates as a unidirectional pipeline that translates narrative intent into rendered video frames:</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Courier&quot;;font-style:normal">Hermes (Master Director Orchestrator)<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”‚<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”‚ High-level narrative intent<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â–¼<br>Scene Contract<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”‚<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”‚ Timing, resolved assets, narration audio<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â–¼<br>Motion Intent<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”‚<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”‚ Editorial motion directives<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â–¼<br>Motion Planner<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”‚<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”‚ Saliency analysis, safe [span_177](start_span)[span_177](end_span)margins, trajectory math<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â–¼<br>Motion Contract (Normalized JSON)<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”‚<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”‚ Structured kinematic parameters<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â–¼<br>Motion / Graphics Worker<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”œâ”€â”€ 2D Sub-Pixel Image Engine (OpenCV / FFmpeg)<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”œâ”€â”€ Vector / Kinetic Typography Engine (Remotion)[span_349](start_span)[span_349](end_span)[span_351](start_span)[span_351](end_span)<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”œâ”€â”€ Vector Micro-Asset Engine (ThorVG)<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â””â”€â”€ Multi-Track Compositing Engine (FFmpeg Filtergraph)<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”‚<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”‚ Synchronized audio &amp; video element streams<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â–¼<br>Canonical Timeline<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”‚<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”‚ Master composition graph<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â–¼<br>Renderer &amp; Hardware Encoder<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”‚<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â”‚ Final encoded delivery file (.mp4)<br> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;â–¼<br>Automated QA Verification<br></span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Stage Responsibilities</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_19-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Hermes</span><span>: Formulates editorial and emotional pacing, emitting semantic motion directives (e.g., </span><span style="font-style:italic">"Slow push-in toward Churchill, somber mood, highlight casualty statistics at 03:20"</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Scene Contract</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Encapsulates audio tracks, resolved image asset paths, voiceover duration, and word alignment data.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Motion Intent</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Extracts motion requirements from the scene contract, specifying visual emphasis points and camera pacing goals.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Motion Planner</span><span>: Ingests visual assets, runs vision pre-flight checks to identify focal points and face coordinates, applies easing equations, validates safe zones, and generates the normalized </span><span style="font-weight:700">Motion Contract</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Motion / Graphics Worker</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Routes contract tracks to specialized execution engines:</span></li></ul><ul class="lst-kix_list_1a-1 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">2D image motion and oversampled camera moves run through optimized OpenCV/FFmpeg sub-pixel workers.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Kinetic captions, dynamic typography, lower thirds, and SVG data graphics run through Remotion inside headless Chromium.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Lottie icons and vector badges are rasterized via the ThorVG engine.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Multi-track alpha compositing, environmental overlay plates, and LUT color grading execute natively in FFmpeg filtergraphs.</span></li></ul><ul class="lst-kix_list_19-0" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Canonical Timeline</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Integrates rendered video plates, transparent graphic streams, and audio tracks into a unified composition graph.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Renderer</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Encodes the final stream using hardware-accelerated FFmpeg pipelines (NVENC/VAAPI) into delivery-compliant H.264/AAC MP4 containers.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Automated QA Verification</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Inspects final media files to verify frame continuity, detect audio/caption drift, ensure loudness compliance (-14 LUFS), and confirm the absence of blank or dropped frames.</span></li></ul><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">26. Sources</span></h2><ul class="lst-kix_list_1b-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">FFmpeg Documentation &amp; Issue Tracker</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Reference documentation for libavfilter, zoompan, scale, overlay, and Trac ticket #4298 tracking coordinate rounding jitter in video cropping pipelines.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Depth Anything Project (Tencent / HKU / ByteDance Seed)</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"